{%- comment -%}
  SYNOR — how many testers, said once.

  This is all that survives of the discovery box. The box's seven empty
  boxes and its progress bar were the wrong shape for the message, but the
  message itself was the only thing on the page that ever said how many to
  take, and without it the page tops out at whatever the shopper first
  reached for.

  It names seven, not three: a number to climb towards. A page that shows a
  set of three teaches people to take three.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign n = count | default: 7 -%}
{%- assign rate = rate | default: 49 -%}
{%- assign sum = n | times: rate -%}
<p class="tstf">
  <b>{{ head | default: 'Seven testers and delivery is free.' }}</b>
  {{ sub | default: 'That is ₹[sum], and every rupee of it comes back.' | replace: '[sum]', sum | replace: '[n]', n }}
</p>
<style>
.tstf{margin:20px 22px 0;padding-top:15px;border-top:1px solid #E5DFD1;
  text-align:center;font-size:11.5px;color:#6E6656;line-height:1.5;
  font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif}
.tstf b{display:block;font-family:'Fraunces',Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;
  font-weight:600;color:#1A1712;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:2px}
@media(min-width:750px){
  .tstf{max-width:720px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}
}
</style>
